
  riscvsim › demo 2 · Waiting for memory
  See why an add must wait one cycle for a load.

   1  # A load reads memory in MEM, one stage later than the
   2  # ALU, so the add right after it must wait one cycle.
   3  .data
   4  value:  .word 41
   5
   6  .text
   7  addi x5, x0, 1     # x5 = 1
   8  # lui puts 0x10000 in the upper 20 bits of x6, so x6
   9  # shows 0x10000000: the address where .data starts.
  10  lui  x6, 0x10000   # x6 = 0x10000000, where value is
  11  lw   x7, 0(x6)     # x7 = 41, read from memory
  12  add  x10, x7, x5   # needs x7 now: one stall

  cycle 1
    IF addi x5, x0, 1  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    › The first instruction, addi, is fetched from memory.

  cycle 2
    IF lui x6, 0x10000  ID addi x5, x0, 1  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    › addi is decoded and reads its source registers.

  cycle 3
    IF lw x7, 0(x6)  ID lui x6, 0x10000  EX addi x5, x0, 1  MEM ·  WB ·
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 4
    IF add x10,x7,x5  ID lw x7, 0(x6)  EX lui x6…  MEM addi x5,x0,1  WB ·
    › lui is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 5
    IF ·  ID add x10,x7,x5  EX lw x7, 0(x6)  MEM lui x6…  WB addi x5,x0,1
    ✓ x5 = 1
    ! lw is reading memory. add must wait one cycle because it needs x7 from
      lw.
      A stall: the instruction stays where it is for a cycle, and an empty
      slot (a bubble) moves on instead.

  cycle 6
    IF ·  ID add x10, x7, x5  EX bubble  MEM lw x7, 0(x6)  WB lui x6, 0x10000
    ✓ x6 = 0x10000000
    › lui finishes and writes x6 = 0x10000000.

  cycle 7
    IF ·  ID ·  EX add x10, x7, x5  MEM bubble  WB lw x7, 0(x6)
    ✓ x7 = 41
    › add needs x7 from lw, so it is forwarded from the MEM/WB pipeline
      register and nobody waits.
      Forwarding: a result goes straight to the instruction that needs it,
      before it is written to its register.
      A pipeline register holds an instruction and its values between two
      stages.

  cycle 8
    IF ·  ID ·  EX ·  MEM add x10, x7, x5  WB bubble
    › Nothing is left to fetch, so the pipeline is emptying.

  cycle 9
    IF ·  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB add x10, x7, x5
    ✓ x10 = 42
    ✓ add writes x10 = 42, and the program is finished.

  ✓ 9 cycles · 4 instructions · CPI 2.25 · 1 stall · 0 mispredictions
    Ends with x5 = 1 · x6 = 0x10000000 · x7 = 41 · x10 = 42
    Why it slowed down:
    • lw is reading memory. add must wait one cycle because it needs x7 from
      lw.

  Next: riscvsim demo 3 (Skipping the wait)